DROP-IN ADD-ONS

Every *.sh file in this directory is sourced by the engine after the kernel has been written and verified, in filename order, with the ui_* helpers and these variables already set:

    BOOT_BLOCK      block device that was written
    PAYLOAD_SIZE    bytes of boot image written
    SLOT            active A/B slot suffix, empty on slotless devices
    KERNEL_NAME     from config.sh
    KERNEL_STRING   from config.sh
    TARGET_PARTITION    from config.sh

Use them for things that are genuinely optional: installing a companion module, writing a tuning profile, printing project-specific notes. An empty directory is the normal case, and a broken add-on is skipped with a warning instead of failing the install.

Anything that must happen for the kernel to work belongs in the engine or in modules/, not here.
